{title: The Purple People Eater}
{artist: Sheb Wooley}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Verse 1 (D)}
[D]Well, I saw the thing comin' out of the sky
It had [A7]one long horn, [D]one big eye (ooh)
I commenced to shakin' and I [G]said, "Ooh-ee"
It [A7]looks like a purple people eater to [D]me

{comment: Chorus}
It was a [D]one-eyed, one-horned, flyin' purple people eater
[A7](One-eyed, one-horned, flyin' purple people eater)
A [D]one-eyed, one-horned, flyin' purple people eater
[A7]Sure looks strange to [D]me (one eye?)

{comment: Verse 2 - modulate up 1/2 step to Eb}
[Eb]Well, he came down to earth and he lit in a tree
I said, [Bb7]"Mr. Purple People Eater, [Eb]don't eat me"
I heard him say in a voice so [Ab]gruff
"I [Bb7]wouldn't eat you 'cause you're so [Eb]tough"

{comment: Chorus}
It was a [Eb]one-eyed, one-horned, flyin' purple people eater
[Bb7]One-eyed, one-horned, flyin' purple people eater
[Eb]One-eyed, one-horned, flyin' purple people eater
[Bb7]Sure looks strange to [Eb]me (one horn?)

{comment: Verse 3 - modulate up 1/2 step to E}
I said, [E]"Mr. Purple People Eater, what's your line?"
He said, [B7]"Eatin' purple people and it [E]sure is fine
But that's not the reason that I came to [A]land
"I [B7]wanna get a job in a rock and roll [E]band"

{comment: Chorus}
Well, bless my soul, rock and roll, flyin' [E]purple people eater
[B7]Pigeon-toed, undergrowed, flyin' purple people eater
[E](We wear short shorts)
Flyin' purple people eater
[B7]Sure looks strange to [E]me (woo)

{comment: Verse 4 (stays in E)}
[E]And then he swung from the tree, and he lit on the ground
And he [B7]started to rock, [E]really rockin' around
It was a crazy ditty with a [A]swingin' tune
Sing a [B7]bop-bap-aboopa-lappa-loom-bam-[E]boom

{comment: Chorus}
Well, bless my soul, rock and roll, flyin' [E]purple people eater
[B7]Pigeon-toed, undergrowed, flyin' purple people eater
[E](I like short shorts)
Flyin' little people eater
[B7]Sure looks strange to [E]me (purple people?)

{comment: Verse 5 - modulate up 1/2 step to F}
Well, [F]he went on his way, and then what do ya know
I saw him [C7]last night on a [F]TV show
He was blowing it out, a-really [Bb]knockin' 'em dead
Playin' [C7]rock and roll music through the horn in his [F]head

[Bb]  [F]  [Bb]  [F]

[F](Tequila)
